## Step 1: Sensing and Mapping
The mobile robot starts by sensing its environment using a combination of sensors such as lidars, cameras, and sonars. These sensors provide the robot with a 2D or 3D representation of its surroundings, including the location of shelves, obstacles, and other relevant features. The robot uses this sensor data to build a map of the warehouse, which is a representation of the environment that the robot can use to plan its path.

